Exp :Perfect Number

Aim:
To write a Java program to check whether a given number is a perfect number or not.

Algorithm:
1. Start the program.
2. Import the Scanner package.
3. Read a number from the user.
4. Initialize sum = 0.
5. Find all proper divisors of the number using a for loop.
6. Add the divisors to the sum.
7. If the sum equals the original number, print Perfect Number; otherwise, print Not a Perfect Number.
8. Stop the program.

Program:

import java.util.Scanner;
public class PerfectNumber {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);

        int n, sum = 0;

        System.out.print("Enter a number: ");
        n = sc.nextInt();

        for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {
            if (n % i == 0) {
                sum = sum + i;
            }
        }

        if (n > 1 && sum == n) {
            System.out.println("Perfect Number");
        } else {
            System.out.println("Not a Perfect Number");
        }

        sc.close();
    }
}

